/-!
# Serre's global generation theorem for ample line bundles

On a quasi-compact quasi-separated scheme `X`, twisting any quasi-coherent `𝒪_X`-module `F` of
finite type by a sufficiently high tensor power of an ample invertible sheaf `L` makes `F ⊗ L^⊗n`
globally generated by finitely many sections: there is an epimorphism `𝒪_X^J ⟶ F ⊗ L^⊗n` from a
free sheaf of finite rank (Hartshorne, Theorem II.5.17; Stacks Project, Tag 01Q3).

The proof proceeds in two steps:

1. **Affine nonvanishing cover.** Suppose `X` is covered by finitely many affine nonvanishing loci
   `X_{sᵢ}` of global sections `sᵢ` of an invertible sheaf `L`. On each affine `X_{sᵢ}`, the
   module `Γ(X_{sᵢ}, F)` is finitely generated. By Hartshorne Lemma II.5.14(b)
   (`Scheme.Modules.exists_map_eq_tmulRight_tensorPowSection`), each generator `t` extends after
   tensoring with some power `sᵢ^k` to a global section of `F ⊗ L^⊗k`. Tensoring repeatedly with
   `sᵢ` lifts these extensions to every degree `n ≥ k`, where multiplication by `sᵢ^n` is an
   isomorphism on `X_{sᵢ}`
   (`Scheme.Modules.bijective_tmulRight_tensorPowSection_of_le_nonvanishingLocus`). Taking `n₀` to
   be the maximum of the exponents `k`, the global extensions generate `F ⊗ L^⊗n` over every affine
   open `X_{sᵢ}`, giving an epimorphism `𝒪_X^J ⟶ F ⊗ L^⊗n`.
2. **General ample line bundle.** By compactness and ampleness of `L`, `X` is covered by finitely
   many affine opens `X_{sᵢ}` with `sᵢ ∈ Γ(X, L^{⊗dᵢ})` and `dᵢ > 0`. Passing to a common
   positive multiple `d = ∏ dᵢ` replaces each `sᵢ` by a positive power in `L^{⊗d}` with the same
   nonvanishing locus (`Scheme.Modules.nonvanishingLocus_tensorPowSection_of_pos`). Applying
   step 1 to `L^{⊗d}` and each of the `d` twists `F ⊗ L^{⊗r}` (`0 ≤ r < d`) yields a uniform
   bound `n₀` for all `n ≥ n₀`.

Applying the theorem to a line bundle `K` shows that `K ⊗ L^{⊗n}` and `L^{⊗n}` are globally
generated for all sufficiently large `n`. Tensoring a surjection `𝒪_X^J ⟶ F ⊗ M` by an inverse
`M'` (`M ⊗ M' ≅ 𝒪_X`) yields an epimorphism `⨁_{j ∈ J} M' ⟶ F`.

## Main results

* `TauCeti.AlgebraicGeometry.InvertibleSheaf.tensorPowObjIso`: identifies `(L.tensorPow n).obj`
  with the monoidal tensor power `TauCeti.tensorPow L.obj n`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.nonvanishingLocus_tensorPowSection_of_pos`: for `0 < q`,
  `X_{s^q} = X_s`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.epi_of_isOpenCover_span_eq_top`: global sections of a
  quasi-coherent sheaf that generate its sections over an affine open cover define an epimorphism
  from the free sheaf.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.exists_epi_free_tensorPow_of_iSup_nonvanishingLocus`:
  finite global generation of `F ⊗ L^{⊗n}` when `X` is covered by finitely many affine `X_{sᵢ}`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.exists_epi_free_tensorPow_of_isAmple`: Serre's global
  generation theorem for an ample line bundle on a quasi-separated scheme.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.biproductConstIsoTensorFree` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.exists_epi_biproduct_of_epi_free_tensor`: dualizing an
  epimorphism `𝒪_X^J ⟶ F ⊗ M` into an epimorphism `⨁_J M' ⟶ F`.
* `TauCeti.AlgebraicGeometry.InvertibleSheaf.exists_isGloballyGenerated_tensorProduct_tensorPow`
  and `exists_isGloballyGenerated_tensorPow`: high ample twists of any line bundle (and high
  powers of an ample line bundle) are globally generated.

## References

* R. Hartshorne, *Algebraic Geometry*, GTM 52, Springer, 1977, Theorem II.5.17.
* [The Stacks Project, Tag 01Q3](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01Q3).
-/

